    "description": {
      "value": "<p>You exert a crushing gravitational pull on a living creature's vital core, compressing and tearing inward. The target takes 8d10 void damage. If this damage reduces the target to 0 Hit Points, it is immediately slain \u2014 its heart (or functional equivalent) is ripped free and appears in your free hand; this is a death effect.</p><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature takes half damage.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature takes full damage.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature takes double damage. If this reduces the creature to 0 Hit Points, it is immediately slain as described above.</p><hr /><p><strong>Heightened (+1)</strong> The damage increases by 1d10.</p>"
